# lane TAIL — Wave-3 remainders (animations, protocol/robustness, error surfaces)
# Worktree .worktrees/lane-tail, branch lane/tail. Append-only lane record.

## Phase 1 — animations (item 1)
- (a) busy tab spinner: SPINNER_FRAMES + spinner_frame_at(clock) — session_tabs.rs; indicator_chunks cycles ⠋⠙⠹… at 80 ms/frame off the store clock (paint_solid_bar_clock); paint_live_tabs_bar now sets busy = store.session_running(id) (context/session-tabs.tsx:170-174). PTY: vt_temporal_marquee un-ignored green; spinner unit covers the full 10-frame cycle at the frozen clock pin.
- (b) TabPulse sweep: tab_pulse.rs gains the full envelope math (RUN_*/COMPLETION_*/GLOW_* constants, intensityAt, coast, attackDecay, blendTabPulseColor, fronts) as PURE functions of TabPulseTrack transition stamps + clock (stateless per frame — no thread-global mutable envelopes; golden frames byte-stable at frozen clock). The strip paints the busy band per cell at 0.14 amplitude over pulseColor=tint(bg,text,0.45) (session-tabs.tsx:1575). Store: tab_pulse_track() stamps busy/glow/completion flips at the clock.
- (c) hover marquee: components/marquee.rs (marqueeCycleWidth/Overflows/TextParts verbatim + deterministic offset: 600 ms delay, +1/80 ms, one cycle then stop; leading fade 250 ms). title_chunks scrolls the hovered overflowing title; VT proof vt_temporal_marquee_shifts_one_cell_per_tick GREEN (was the registered ignored v2 gap).
- (d) title_shimmer envelope: store title_pending (armed at the rename POST, released by the session.renamed/updated echo — context/data.tsx:35-42 semantics); sidebar title paints the sustained segment (dim 40% toward the backdrop, 1200 ms coasting highlight band, 240 ms blend-in) as per-char runs in render_sidebar_scrolled.
- (e) scrim alpha: session.rs apply_scrim — rgba(0,0,0,70) composited over the route content (per-cell bg blend toward black at 70/255); the composer echo survives under the manual-open overlay (the registered 2026-10-12 "no echo" seam). Test updated accordingly.
- Budget pair: animated_strip_stays_inside_the_frame_budget — 12 busy tabs, 60 live-clock frames, worst < 40 ms (measured ~1 ms class).
- Verification: cargo nextest -p oc-tui 787/787 green (incl. all goldens); clippy -D warnings clean; fmt applied.

## Phase 2 — protocol/robustness (item 2, auditC)
- New module terminal_proto.rs — byte-exact sequences + tests: kitty query/push/pop (CSI ?u / CSI >5u / CSI <u), theme subscriptions ?2027h+?2031h, DECSCUSR matrix + OSC 12, kitty graphics a=d,d=a delete-all, the editor paste/focus handoff pair, crash-restore sequences (mouse-gated), clipboard read (host tools + OSC 52 query + parse + image sniff/mime).
- P2/TM-1 kitty negotiation: the boot probe (theme.rs probe_terminal — one combined 300ms window, OSC 11 + CSI ?u) parses the advertisement (parse_kitty_advertisement); run loop pushes CSI >5u when advertised; teardown pops CSI <u. PTY proof pty_kitty_handshake_and_teardown_bytes: answering terminal → push asserted; teardown pop + cursor reset asserted. (crossterm 0.28 has NO public Event variant for the CSI ?flags u reply — the answer is parsed in the boot window, not the event stream.)
- P6/TM-2 theme subs: ?2027h+?2031h emitted at boot (PTY-asserted). The ?997;1n/2n notifications are UNDELIVERABLE through crossterm's CSI parser (only ?u/?c dispatch; ?997 swallowed) — behavioral stand-in: focus-triggered OSC 11 re-probe (10s cooldown, mode=="system" only, query_terminal_background_in_raw — no raw-mode toggling mid-loop) refreshing the palette live. Registered divergence.
- P7/TM-3 cursor styling: DECSCUSR from the new cursor config doc (oc-core Info.cursor consumed via TuiConfig::from_info; style block/underline/line/default × blinking, default blink-block = CSI 1 SP q) + OSC 12 with the theme text color at boot; CSI 0 q reset at teardown.
- P8 clipboard read: host-first (pbpaste/xclip/xsel/wl-paste) wired into prompt.paste (ctrl+v) — image bytes sniffed (PNG/JPEG/GIF/WEBP) stage as a "clipboard" data-URI attachment chip, text inserts (v2 prompt/index.tsx:474-491). The OSC 52 terminal read arm is IMPLEMENTED + unit-tested (query bytes, reply parser incl. refusal, image magic) but NOT wired live: crossterm's input thread owns stdin, a query window would race it and eat keystrokes — v2's renderer owns its input pipeline, we do not. Registered deferral.
- P3 panic/signal restore: install_crash_restore — SIGHUP/SIGTERM handlers (write(2)-only + _exit, async-signal-safe) + a chained panic hook writing the full restore sequence (alt-screen leave, ?1004l/?2004l, mouse pops gated by the live AtomicBool, kitty pop, cursor reset). PTY proof pty_panic_mid_run_restores_the_terminal: a thread panicking mid-render → the restore bytes observed on the pty (occurrence-count watch — an offset watch races the reader chunking).
- P11 BEL: gated behind attention.bell (default FALSE — v2 never emits BEL); oc-core AttentionInfo + TuiConfig carry the flag.
- P12 editor suspend: ?2004/?1004 pop before $EDITOR + re-push after (with the mouse pair).
- P13: the promised kitty graphics a=d,d=a delete-all now actually emitted at teardown when a graphics protocol was detected.
- Config: oc-core Info gains AttentionInfo.bell (cursor already existed); oc-tui TuiConfig gains cursor: CursorConfig (both parse paths).
- Verification: oc-tui 1647-test run green (1 pre-existing oc-core test-target clippy debt noted, unrelated files); PTY proofs green; clippy -D clean on oc-tui all-targets + oc-core lib.

## Phase 3 — error/updater surfaces (item 3, auditB #9/#10 + SURF-2 deferrals)
- New components/update.rs: UpdateNotice (kind/version/remote + notice-file line parser + banner copy per home.tsx:153-170), UpdateDialogState (checking/current/available/installing/installed/failed/unavailable + dialog rows + confirm labels), error_component_frame (the ErrorComponent crash fallback).
- #10 updater: store update_notice/update_dialog/update_dismissed signals; notify respects the dismissed `source:version` history (persisted — storage KEY_UPDATE_NOTIFICATIONS, the last-100 v2 shape) and client-never-displaces-server; SSE `installation.update-available`/`installation.updated` arms (update-notification.tsx:113-121); the CLI checker's notice file (`<state>/update-notice.log`) read at boot + mtime-watched per tick (the local `updater.subscribe`); /update command + DialogKind::Update (select: state row + Skip/Update/Restart; confirm → Installing via the ServerPending seam → the loop spawns `current_exe upgrade` with stdio appended to the notice file — Installing→Installed rides the same file watch; Restart exits); home UpdateNotification banner (centered row above the prompt, `/update`/`/exit` prefix in action.primary.selected, remote variant copy) — golden fixtures unchanged (banner None).
- #9 errors: ErrorComponent — the run loop wraps app.frame() in catch_unwind; a render panic swaps in the sticky fallback frame (store-independent paint), the terminal-owner panic hook restores the terminal, any key exits (PTY proof pty_render_panic_shows_the_error_component_and_exits via OC_TUI_TEST_RENDER_PANIC=N); ThemeErrorToast — a configured/selected theme that fails to resolve errors visibly (boot apply_config + the theme dialog submit); MCP needs-auth/failed toasts: ALREADY landed (lane KM, verified set_mcp_servers alerting).
- Panic-hook refinement: the hook now restores ONLY on the terminal-owner thread (worker-thread panics are routinely caught — the plugin host — and must not tear the terminal mid-run); the worker-crash PTY test retired in favor of the owner-thread render-crash proof.
- Verification: oc-tui 802/802 green; clippy -D clean; PTY proofs green.
- DEFERRALS (documented): MigrationOverlay — no v1 migration API exists in the Rust stack (oc-server runs a synchronous one-way v2→rust migration at boot, nothing to poll); SessionLocationMissing — needs a location-error source in the store (the location worker never errors into state today — a separate seam); pair QR block — needs a QR encoder (no dep exists; SURF-2's deferral stands); DiffViewerImage halfblock preview — needs the image-decode plumbing into the diff viewer path; the banner's hover-lift/pointer-click (the /update command reaches the dialog today).
